* 25 Oct 26 Windows port - from Linux fc4030a (S.66, the shared account): SHARED-READ-ON / SHARED-READ-OFF and SHARED-WRITE-ON / SHARED-WRITE-OFF, the two
*   gates for the files of the group account named shared.  Allowed on a group account (and on the account shared itself: the words on THAT account decide
*   what the members of its group can do inside it).  Account-scoped: they take effect at the person's next account entry.  The register says 'yes' or
*   'no' (a decided state); read is ON when the field is blank, so SHARED-READ-OFF must write 'no' even to a blank record (os.set's os.was).
      case action = 'SHARED-READ-ON'
